@host = http://localhost:5253

### All customers
GET {{host}}/customers

### Create a customer
POST {{host}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Linus Torvalds",
  "email": "linus@example.com"
}

### Same email again — 2601 from the unique index, surfaced as 500 (no error handling on purpose)
POST {{host}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Linus Again",
  "email": "linus@example.com"
}

### ---- Week 6 Wednesday: transactions ----
### 0. Reset: StockCount = 10, no shipments
POST {{host}}/shipments/reset

### 1. Naive, happy path: two SaveChanges, works (StockCount 8, one shipment)
POST {{host}}/shipments?version=naive
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### 2. Naive + crash: StockCount 8 but NO shipment — 2 keyboards gone (run 0 first)
POST {{host}}/shipments?version=naive&crash=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### 3. Transaction + crash: rollback, StockCount back at 10 (run 0 first)
POST {{host}}/shipments?version=transaction&crash=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### 4. Final: one SaveChanges, validation first → 201
POST {{host}}/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### 5. Final: too many → 409 before any transaction is opened
POST {{host}}/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 20 }

### 6. Final: unknown product → 404
POST {{host}}/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 999, "quantity": 1 }

### Look at the state
GET {{host}}/products

###
GET {{host}}/shipments
